-- One key press, answering `ReadKey` (spec §11.6). A sum type, so that a program handles keys
-- by name and `match` checks it. Malformed input is `Other`, so `Char` is always a valid CHAR.
-- `Ctrl(c)` is Ctrl with a letter, given as the lowercase letter, apart from the chords that are
-- keys of their own: Ctrl-H is Backspace, Ctrl-I Tab, Ctrl-J and Ctrl-M Enter.
-- `Function(n)` is F1 to F12, `n` from 1 to 12.
-- `Mod(key, shift, alt, ctrl)` is a key pressed with Shift, Alt or Ctrl, at least one of them:
-- Shift-Tab, Ctrl-Right, Shift-Home, Alt-x. Its key is never a `Mod`, `Ctrl`, `Other` or
-- `KeysEnded`, and a `Char` only with Alt, as Shift is in the character already. A program
-- that does not list `Mod` takes these keys in its `case _`.
module KEY

representation {ANY}
  | Char(c: CHAR)
  | Up
  | Down
  | Left
  | Right
  | Enter
  | Escape
  | Backspace
  | Tab
  | Home
  | End
  | PageUp
  | PageDown
  | Delete
  | Ctrl(c: CHAR)
  | Other
  | KeysEnded
  | Insert
  | Function(n: NAT)
  | Mod(key: KEY, shift: BOOL, alt: BOOL, ctrl: BOOL)

end
